{"value": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/servicecomb-java-chassis/pulls/3501", "id": 1135404090, "node_id": "PR_kwDOBXbZOM5DrOQ6", "html_url": "https://github.com/apache/servicecomb-java-chassis/pull/3501", "diff_url": "https://github.com/apache/servicecomb-java-chassis/pull/3501.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/apache/servicecomb-java-chassis/pull/3501.patch", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/servicecomb-java-chassis/issues/3501", "commits_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/servicecomb-java-chassis/pulls/3501/commits", "review_comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/servicecomb-java-chassis/pulls/3501/comments", "review_comment_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/servicecomb-java-chassis/pulls/comments{/number}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/servicecomb-java-chassis/issues/3501/comments", "statuses_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/servicecomb-java-chassis/statuses/fe65835286e91248b450da17a28e49c44bae8e30", "number": 3501, "state": "closed", "locked": false, "title": "[SCB-2731] fix flaky junit tests in common and core", "user": {"login": "anantdahiya8", "id": 20678029, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjc4MDI5", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20678029?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/anantdahiya8", "html_url": "https://github.com/anantdahiya8", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/anantdahiya8/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/anantdahiya8/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/anantdahiya8/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/anantdahiya8/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/anantdahiya8/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/anantdahiya8/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/anantdahiya8/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/anantdahiya8/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/anantdahiya8/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "### Summary\r\n\r\n1. `TestInvocation#traceIdGeneratorInit`\r\n- Using `containsInAnyOrder` so that the junit test passes for every order of the values \r\n<hr />\r\n\r\n2. `TestRestClientRequestImpl#testForm`\r\n-  Checking all possible values so that the test does not fail\r\n<hr />\r\n\r\n3. `TestRestClientRequestImpl#testCookie`\r\n- Mocking for both cases `\"region=china-north; sessionid=abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz; \"` and `\"sessionid=abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz; region=china-north; \"`, So that the mock function works for both the cases\r\n<hr />\r\n\r\n4. `RestServerCodecFilterTest#should_convert_exception_to_response_when_decode_request_failed`\r\n- `Json.encode` can return the json string in different order. We need to check for all the possible values so that the test does not fail for some cases.\r\n<hr />\r\n\r\n5. `RestProducerInvocationCreatorTest#should_failed_when_not_defined_any_schema`\r\n- `Json.encode` can return the json string in different order. We need to check for all the possible values so that the test does not fail for some cases.\r\n<hr />\r\n\r\n6. `RestProducerInvocationCreatorTest#should_failed_when_accept_is_not_support`\r\n- `Json.encode` can return the json string in different order. We need to check for all the possible values so that the test does not fail for some cases.\r\n<hr />\r\n\r\nBug Link : https://issues.apache.org/jira/projects/SCB/issues/SCB-2731\r\n\r\nFollow this checklist to help us incorporate your contribution quickly and easily:\r\n\r\n - [x] Make sure there is a [JIRA issue](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/SCB) filed for the change (usually before you start working on it).  Trivial changes like typos do not require a JIRA issue.  Your pull request should address just this issue, without pulling in other changes.\r\n - [x] Each commit in the pull request should have a meaningful subject line and body.\r\n - [x] Format the pull request title like `[SCB-XXX] Fixes bug in ApproximateQuantiles`, where you replace `SCB-XXX` with the appropriate JIRA issue.\r\n - [x] Write a pull request description that is detailed enough to understand what the pull request does, how, and why.\r\n - [x] Run `mvn clean install -Pit` to make sure basic checks pass. A more thorough check will be performed on your pull request automatically.\r\n - [x] If this contribution is large, please file an Apache [Individual Contributor License Agreement](https://www.apache.org/licenses/icla.pdf).\r\n\r\n---\r\n", "labels": [], "milestone": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "created_at": "2022-11-25T00:05:30Z", "updated_at": "2022-11-26T09:22:00Z", "closed_at": "2022-11-26T01:54:44Z", "merged_at": "2022-11-26T01:54:44Z", "merge_commit_sha": "ad0b38f9de90c73526fed719fd5dba6430e653b2", "assignee": null, "assignees": [], "requested_reviewers": [], "requested_teams": [], "head": {"label": "anantdahiya8:fix-flaky-core-common", "ref": "fix-flaky-core-common", "repo": {"id": 540964272, "node_id": "R_kgDOID51sA", "name": "servicecomb-java-chassis", "full_name": "anantdahiya8/servicecomb-java-chassis", "owner": {"login": "anantdahiya8", "id": 20678029, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjc4MDI5", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20678029?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/anantdahiya8", "html_url": "https://github.com/anantdahiya8", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/anantdahiya8/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/anantdahiya8/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/anantdahiya8/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/anantdahiya8/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/anantdahiya8/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/anantdahiya8/orgs", "repos_url": "